<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT WALES 34-13.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT WALES 34-13.</headline>
<dateline>CARDIFF 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>England beat Wales 34-13 (halftime 6-3) on Saturday in their final Five Nations' championship match.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Tries: Tim Stimpson, Tony Underwood, Richard Hill, Phil de Glanville. Penalties: Mike Catt (2). Conversions: Catt (4).</p>
<p>Wales - Try: Rob Howley. Penalties: Jonathan Davies (2). Conversion. Davies</p>
</text>
